pst-numeric: changes

1.2  2026/11/21  first release on CTAN
                 - the library is now the PSTricks package pst-numeric
                   (tex/pst-numeric.tex, latex/pst-numeric.sty), with
                   options to load only some parts, \pstNumeric,
                   \psNumericShow and a manual
                 - every name is defined in the dictionary tx@NumericDict
                   instead of userdict; Load.ps opens it, so code that
                   starts with (Load.ps) run works unchanged
                 - each part is a dvips header in dvips/, generated by
                   source/make_headers.py
                 - the repository is renamed pst-numeric (it was
                   postscript-math) and its files are sorted into
                   source/, test/, examples/ and tools/
                 - 6 new tests for the namespace (581 in all); the tests
                   run against the .ps files and the headers, and pass
                   with Ghostscript 9.52 and 10.08

1.1  2026/11     (as postscript-math)
                 - Matrix.ps: mfromrows, mtorows, mcopy, midentity,
                   mtranspose, madd, msub, mscale, mdet, minv, msolve,
                   mlstsq, meigsym, mPrint; every operation accepts bignum
                   and decimal-string elements
                 - bignumlibrary.ps: sqrtbn, expbn, powbn, atanbn, asinbn,
                   acosbn, atan2bn, sinhbn, coshbn, tanhbn, factbn,
                   binombn; typchk recognises complex numbers
                 - new: Complex.ps (complex numbers) and Numeric.ps (roots,
                   integrals, polynomials, gcd and lcm)
                 - 253 new tests (575 in all)

1.0  2026/11     (as postscript-math)
                 - bignumlibrary.ps rewritten with the same number format;
                   subbn, mulbn and setbn fixed; added divbn, the
                   comparisons, negbn, absbn, truncbn, roundbn, bniszero,
                   bncvs, bncvr, sinbn, cosbn, tanbn, lnbn, log10bn, pibn;
                   default precision 20 digits
                 - Trig.ps rewritten from the CORDIC algorithm; fixes the
                   signs of corcos and cortan and coratan for x > 0, y < 0
                 - Matrix.ps: removed a stray showpage
                 - licensed under the LPPL 1.3c

0.5  2012        first version (bignumlibrary.ps, Trig.ps, Matrix.ps)
